# Global rules (every zone, every session)

Read `CLAUDE.md` first, every session. It maps docs and locations.
Company is **AETRYX LTD** (replaces NULLSPACE LABS everywhere new).

## Discipline

- **One zone per session.** Declare scope up front; never touch files outside it.
- **Phase plan first**, then implement phase by phase.
- Commit after every completed phase: `feat(zone): phase N — summary`.
  Push to the current feature branch. Never push directly to `main` — merges
  go through PR review by the architect.
- If a spec forces deviation: STOP, note it in the final report, add an ADR
  in `docs/decisions/` if you decided something. No silent improvisation.

## Vocabulary & brand

- Use ONLY glossary terms (`docs/50-GLOSSARY.md`): Figure, Case, Mint, Run,
  Shards, PX, Dissolve, Open Ritual, Museum, Passport, Vault/Gallery.
  Never "lootbox", "NFT", "burn" in UI copy.
- Voice: museum curator, not casino barker. Sentence case. No exclamation
  marks in system UI. Numbers are heroes.
- Design law is The POXY Codex (`docs/10-BRAND.md`, Still Water). The
  casino-test and its forbidden list apply to every UI change.
- **Rarity pigments appear ONLY in gem SVGs, rarity badges and the reveal
  glow** — never on layout, surfaces, buttons or text.

## Safety (outranks features and speed)

- Client never holds secrets, service-role keys, or authoritative
  prices/odds/yields. Server reads them from the DB.
- Every balance change goes through the ledger tables. No exceptions.
- Crypto engine (commit-reveal RNG, SHA-256 identity hashes, ED25519,
  Merkle) is server-side only and append-only.
- 18+ gate, spending limits, self-exclusion are server-enforced. Never
  weaken RLS.
- `archive/prototype-v1/` is the still-deployed legacy product: hotfixes
  only, never restructure it.
